# Fork job

Read [docs/FORK.md](../../docs/FORK.md) before changing how this fork treats UiPath. The rationale lives there. This rule only keeps the boundary.

This fork is structural recall for UiPath projects: overview, outline, who uses a name, invoke chain, impact, and lint. The model spends tokens on the answer, not on walking XAML.

The UiPath skills and the `uip` CLI author and run. Do not port UiPathEngineeringMCP.

XAML-majority: at least 75% of the automation stays in `.xaml`. Coded workflows are the exception. Do not add findings that tell the agent to move business logic into C#.

Decisions stay in the project kit's `docs/adr`, not in `manage_adr`.

```text
# Every session in this repo:
Read docs/FORK.md. Recall structure from the graph.
# Author and run:
UiPath skills and `uip`. Decisions go in the project kit's docs/adr.
# Leave parked:
UiPathEngineeringMCP. No finding that moves business logic into C#.
```
